  "notes": "{偽造|ぎぞう} refers to creating a fake version of something from scratch with intent to deceive. A legal and criminal term.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {偽造|ぎぞう}{紙幣|しへい}: counterfeit banknotes\n- {偽造|ぎぞう}パスポート: forged passport\n- {文書|ぶんしょ}{偽造|ぎぞう}: document forgery\n- {偽造|ぎぞう}{品|ひん}: counterfeit goods\n- {偽造|ぎぞう}{防止|ぼうし}: anti-counterfeiting\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {改竄|かいざん}: tampering, falsification (altering an existing document)\n- {偽物|にせもの}: fake, counterfeit (the resulting item)\n- {模造|もぞう}: imitation (not always illegal — e.g., {模造|もぞう}{品|ひん} can be a legal replica)\n- {捏造|ねつぞう}: fabrication (especially of facts or data)",
